/E (Every law creates a risk for abuse. This does not mean that the issue should not be regulated or legislated, but rather that in designing, interpreting, and implementing legislation, there should be control mechanisms built in to counter eventual abuse. These often vary depending on cultural and historical issues. Some states are more prone to corruption, others to despotism or authoritarianism, others to armed conflict or war, etc. These risks can be unpacked in the following way:)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
